:"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkxMjgwNDQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/confirmed","name":"confirmed","color":"aaddaa","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1609442062,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNjA5NDQyMDYy","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:shaders","name":"topic:shaders","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/22","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/22","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/22/labels","id":12070367,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AuC3f","number":22,"title":"4.5","description":"","creator":{"login":"Sauermann","id":6299227,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyOTkyMjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6299227?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann","html_url":"https://github.com/Sauermann","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":3,"closed_issues":3687,"state":"closed","created_at":"2024-12-19T08:51:28Z","updated_at":"2026-09-04T21:48:38Z","due_on":"2025-09-15T00:00:00Z","closed_at":"2025-09-18T17:13:14Z"},"comments":0,"created_at":"2025-06-25T16:53:40Z","updated_at":"2025-07-09T16:40:09Z","closed_at":"2025-07-09T16:38:33Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in; v4.4.1\n(Shader function overload was not available prior so no bug to test there)\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable (49a5bc7b6) - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 6950 XT (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 32.0.21013.1000) - AMD Ryzen 9 5900X 12-Core Processor (24 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nUsing function overload on shaders to use the same function name with diferent possible arguments, return options creates a shader error if the first function definition has more arguments than later ones.\n\nThe following code will create an error in shader stating the posterize needs 3 arguments if we try to use the second definition. \n```\nvoid posterize(in vec4 in_value, in vec4 steps, out vec4 out_value)\n{\n\tout_value = floor(in_value * steps) / steps;\n}\n\nvec4 posterize(in vec4 in_value, in vec4 steps)\n{\n\treturn floor(in_value * steps) / steps;\n}\n```\n\nCalling the second function (2 arguments) later in the fragment shader creates the following error\n```\n60 - Too few arguments for \"posterize(vec4, vec4, vec4)\" call. Expected at least 3 but received 2.\n```\n\nAs a note the shader editor detects the 2 functions defined \n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8c234660-16e0-4da1-90e7-1064db02390f)\n\n\nThe code works fine sapping the order of the defintions, something like this code below will compile and work fine:\n```\nvec4 posterize(in vec4 in_value, in vec4 steps)\n{\n\treturn floor(in_value * steps) / steps;\n}\n\nvoid posterize(in vec4 in_value, in vec4 steps, out vec4 out_value)\n{\n\tout_value = floor(in_value * steps) / steps;\n}\n```\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create a shader function with 3 arguments.\n- Create the same shader function with 2 arguments, overloading the one you just created.\n- Try to use the second function in fragment shader.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[shaderoverloaderror.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20907803/shaderoverloaderror.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107982/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107982/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}